title: LSP

!! Language Server Protocol

The `--lsp` command serves your editor from the booted wiki: completion, hovers, go to definition, find references, rename and more for `.tid` files. VS Code starts it for you, as a child of the window, see [[LSP Configuration]].

It keeps in step with a running MCP server, so a tiddler an assistant has just created is a title your editor offers moments later, and a save in the editor reaches the browser.

